// "[subject] isn't [predicate]" — [`SubjectIs`]'s negation twin:
// `Not(Matches(<subject>, <predicate>))`. See `SubjectIs` for the shared
// `Param(0)`/`Param(1)` vocabulary and the render note (a hand-written
// `Condition::Not(Matches(..))` arm, not the generic template filler).
//
// Usage: SubjectIsnt(AttachHostOf(This), Supertype(Legendary)).
(
    name: "SubjectIsnt",
    template: "${0} isn't ${1}",
    kinds: [Condition],
    params: [Reference, Predicate],
    body: Not(Matches(Param(0), Param(1))),
)
